    fullDescription: "All'Antico Vinaio is the most famous sandwich shop in Florence and arguably in all Italy, a phenomenon that has grown from a humble wine-and-panini bar founded in 1991 on Via dei Neri into a global name with branches abroad, yet the original still draws snaking queues down the street all day long. The product that made its reputation is deceptively simple: a huge slab of freshly baked schiacciata — the soft, olive-oil-rich Tuscan flatbread — split and crammed to order with combinations of top-quality cured meats, pecorino and other cheeses, grilled and marinated vegetables, and the addictive truffle-cream and artichoke-cream spreads that give the sandwiches their cult following. The best-known combination, 'La Favolosa', layers spicy salami, pecorino, aubergine and artichoke cream, but you can point at the ingredients behind the counter and build your own. Portions are enormous and the price, at well under ten euros for a sandwich that easily feeds one hungry person or two lighter appetites, makes it one of the best-value lunches in a pricey city. The catch is the queue, which can be long, though it usually moves faster than it looks as the staff assemble sandwiches at speed; there are now several branches within a few doors of each other on the same street to spread the load. There is little seating, so most people eat standing or carry their sandwich to the steps of a nearby piazza or the riverbank. For a fast, cheap, delicious and quintessentially Florentine bite between sights, it is a rite of passage.",
