    fullDescription: "The Palazzo Vecchio, Florence's grand medieval town hall on Piazza della Signoria, runs one of the best programmes of family activities of any museum in the city, transforming what could be a dry tour of state rooms into a genuinely exciting adventure that captivates children. The palace's education department offers a series of themed guided tours and workshops designed specifically for families and kids, which must be booked in advance and are well worth planning around. The most popular is the 'secret passages' tour, which takes small groups through hidden doors, concealed staircases and normally off-limits spaces — including the cavity above the ceiling of the vast Salone dei Cinquecento, where you can see the massive wooden roof structure — revealing the intrigue, escape routes and hidden machinery of the Medici court in a way that thrills children with its sense of mystery and discovery. Other activities include costumed role-play tours where kids dress up and meet characters from the Medici era, learning about life at the Renaissance court, and creative workshops. Beyond the organised activities, the palace itself is atmospheric and rewarding for families, with its enormous frescoed hall, opulent chambers, maps and the climb up the Arnolfo Tower for a great view over the piazza. Being centrally located and largely indoors, it also makes an excellent rainy-day option. Booking the family tours ahead is essential, as places are limited and they are deservedly popular. For turning Renaissance history into an interactive, imaginative experience that engages children rather than boring them, the Palazzo Vecchio's family programme is one of the smartest and most memorable things to do with kids in Florence.",
